			"color":"#232",
			"widgets_values":[
				" subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the young swordswoman in <Picture 1>, with long black hair styled in a traditional half-updo adorned with small white flower hairpins, delicate facial features, and wearing a flowing white sheer ancient Chinese hanfu dress with wide sleeves.\n<Subject 2> is the watermelon stall in <Picture 1>, featuring multiple whole and halved watermelons with bright red flesh, bamboo display stands, woven baskets, and wooden poles.\n<Subject 3> is the ancient Chinese street background in <Picture 1>, with wooden architecture, grey brick walls, and blurred pedestrians in traditional clothing in the distance.\n<Subject 4> is the sword in <Picture 1>, a short straight blade with a brass hilt, held in the woman's right hand.\n<Picture 1> is the reference image for character appearance, costume, watermelon stall setting, ancient street environment, and overall cinematic wuxia aesthetic.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation] The target video is a 10-second wuxia short drama featuring <Subject 1> the white-clad swordswoman at <Subject 2> the watermelon stall on <Subject 3> the ancient street. She draws and swings <Subject 4> her sword with precise martial arts technique, cleanly slicing a watermelon in half, then calmly resheathes the blade with a faint confident smile.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 2], [Shot 3]): fully_preserved - the swordswoman's facial features, hairstyle with white flower pins, and flowing white hanfu dress are fully retained.\n<Subject 2> (appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 2], [Shot 3]): partially_preserved - the watermelon stall, bamboo stands, and most watermelons are retained; one watermelon is sliced open by the sword during the action.\n<Subject 3> (appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 2], [Shot 3]): fully_preserved - the ancient street background with wooden buildings and distant pedestrians is fully retained.\n<Subject 4> (appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 2], [Shot 3]): fully_preserved - the short sword with brass hilt is fully retained.\n<Picture 1> (overall style reference): fully_preserved - the soft natural lighting, warm cinematic color palette, shallow depth of field, and photorealistic wuxia drama quality are fully retained.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video uses a cinematic wuxia drama style with soft natural daylight, warm color grading, shallow depth of field, and photorealistic texture.\n[Shot 1] A medium shot establishes <Subject 1> the white-clad swordswoman standing beside <Subject 2> the watermelon stall on <Subject 3> the ancient street. She holds <Subject 4> the short sword in her right hand in a ready stance, her left sleeve extended outward. Her expression is calm and alert as she gazes slightly off-camera. A gentle breeze stirs her long hair and the flowing white fabric of her wide sleeves. The camera holds a static shot as she slowly tightens her grip on the sword hilt, her eyes narrowing with focus.\n[Shot 2] At 00:03.000, the shot cuts to a dynamic medium shot capturing the sword strike. <Subject 1> draws the blade in a fluid, precise motion — a clean horizontal slash with her right arm extended. The sword glints in the daylight as it moves, leaving a faint trail of light. Her white sleeves billow dramatically with the momentum of the strike. The camera pans right with small amplitude at fast speed, following the arc of the blade. A watermelon on <Subject 2> the stall is cleanly sliced through its equator, the two halves beginning to separate as juice glistens on the freshly cut red flesh.\n[Shot 3] At 00:06.500, the shot cuts back to a medium shot of <Subject 1> as she completes the motion, smoothly resheathing <Subject 4> the sword with practiced elegance. In front of her on <Subject 2> the stall, the perfectly halved watermelon sits with its bright red flesh exposed, cleanly cut with surgical precision. A single drop of juice slowly rolls down the cut surface. The corners of her lips lift into a faint, confident smile as she gazes at the result. The breeze continues to gently move her hair and sleeves. The camera slowly pulls out with small amplitude at slow speed, revealing more of the ancient street scene as the video ends.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nGentle street ambience with distant footsteps and faint market chatter. The sword makes a sharp whooshing sound as it cuts through the air, followed by the clean, crisp sound of the watermelon being sliced open. Soft fabric rustle as the sleeves move.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nTraditional Chinese instrumental score with guzheng and bamboo flute at a moderate tempo, building slightly during the sword strike then settling back into a calm, elegant melody. Subtle percussion accents the moment of the cut."
